 succeeded in 0ms:
    91	Seln came in and sat down at the door end, and that was all that those two had ever said to each other, and it was, Cael thought, more than most men managed in a life.
    92	
    93	Vastin sat. Nobody had told him to. He sat at the table's end, and put his hands flat on the wood, and Cael saw Oryn, across from him, look at the hands, and then at the knee under the table, and then at the face — the count, and the finding — and say nothing, because the finding was hers and she had not been asked for it.
    94	
    95	"I'll say the short thing first," Vastin said. "I am no longer the Compact's. I resigned, or I walked out, and I have spent a winter deciding which and have decided that the distinction is one only the Compact would care about, and I no longer file with them. I have no rank. I have no seal. I have no warrant, no team, no clerk, and no one behind me. I am aware of what that makes me at this table. I have had three hundred miles to be aware of it."
    96	
    97	Nobody said anything. Brom looked at the boots.
    98	
    99	"The long thing." He did not open the pack. His hands stayed on the table. "Before I left, I read the Compact's classified history. All of it that I could reach with what I had, which was more than anyone has reached in a long time, because I had forty years of keys and I used every one of them on the way out. Most of it is what you would expect. Two things are not." He looked at Karis, because Karis had leaned forward, a finger's width, and he had seen it. "A name. And a locked layer."
   100	
   101	Brom spoke before she could. Brom priced things, and he had been pricing this one since the landing, and he said it to the table and not to the man, because that was how a price was said. "He walked here. Alone. In spring mud, on that knee, with a pack he mended himself." He looked at the boots once more. "Three hundred miles is a demonstration. Out here that's the only kind there is." And that was the whole of Brom's price, and it was, from Brom, an argument for hearing a man out and not one hair past it.
   102	
