   174	
   175	He walked through it. On the near shingle a flat boat lay with its bottom stove in, and two black posts leaned beside it. A board had been left face upward in the grass. The paint had gone out of its letters, but they had been cut before they were painted. *Foot. Horse. Cart, loaded.* At the head of it was the registry's seal.
   176	
