   381	- Karis (B7 edition `chapter-57.md:99`; `chapter-60.md:251`): `Three points make a line. Four make an argument.` / `Someone made this pattern.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 8]
   382	- Oryn (B7 edition `chapter-58.md:51–55`; `chapter-60.md:215,229`): `Find me at Thornwater.` / `Bring the map.` Her letter: `Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.` / `Six, by letter.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
   383	- Hesk's straightedge note (B7 edition `chapter-60.md:67`): `Nineteen. I'm told it's late; the ferry's fault, not mine. Your grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. This one's true to a hair. Mind the shape. — H.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 8]
   384	- Teague and Pike (B7 edition `chapter-59.md:199,221–225`): `After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes.` / `Noted.` / `I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
