editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:1:# EVENT LIST — Book 8, Movement 2 "No Sanction" (chapters 7–12, days 271–277 past the Line)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:7:- The night of the 270th at Lowmarch. Six at the lower inn: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, and Oryn, who is on her own road and takes no sixth place. Teague's five at the upper inn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:8:- Cael: nineteen; no Path; ten fragments; **deployment since the Line twenty-nine**; Shadow twice and sealed; Anchor twice, once each way; Tide used on nobody but Oryn (twice) and himself (three times); the still place untouched; the ruling *hold* on the cord and the two edges (he has touched none of the three since the 168th).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:9:- Lira: left arm released on the 266th, slow, not to be fallen on; right ankle mended the same day; the carter's great boot. Brom: right shoulder in the older healer's webbing; she says when. Karis: the case made on the 268th and not answered; fifty-two sheets, the hide, the kit, the dead man's ledger, one hair. Seln: the case shut; forty notches on his second wand (a hundred and forty days since the clerk's packet went over).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:10:- Money: **a hundred and eighteen in hand, and it must still be a hundred and eighteen at the movement's end** (the map's cash spine goes 118 → 138 with the clearance slip on the 278th–279th). Owed: sixty yards of four-strand rope to the ferryman, who will take a rope and no silver; one reed hurdle; a letter to Ephram for the first boat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:14:- Vastin, from Book 6: the Archmarshal, the certifying office; declined to certify; "I am not with anyone"; never exchanged a word with Seln; has never been told what Cael carries. The five's rule from the borrowed room: he gets the case, nothing about Cael.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:19:2. **The rope is not bought in this movement.** The first boat carries people and no goods in that water; the cordage stays on the western landing. The debt stands, and it is why the ferry has only one hauling line when she needs two.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:20:3. **The cutaway comes before the ferry**, at the end of chapter 8, headed with its day, and names him. The reader knows who is on the far bank; Cael does not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:24:## The sums that must add up on the page
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:26:- **Days:** 271 (the scow goes in; the hearing) · 272 (Oryn's bench; the cloth; Teague) · 273 (the bout) · 274 (the hurdle) · 275 (the last shelf goes; the letter) · 276 (the flood; "tomorrow") · 277 (first light: the first boat; the plank; noon: the long table; after noon: the ferry goes west; evening: the back room). Vastin's window: the 265th (the last station) to the evening of the 276th (the western landing), twelve days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:27:- **Seln's second wand:** forty on the 270th; forty-one on the 271st; forty-seven on the 277th: a hundred and forty-seven days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:29:- **Money:** a hundred and eighteen, unchanged. Vastin pays his own fare (a copper), his own bread (a copper and a half) and his own bowl (a copper).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:32:- **The scow:** nine aboard coming east: the ferryman and eight passengers.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:42:1. **The scow goes in (271, morning).** The ferryman and his boy walk her down the greased slip on rollers; the shelf ice is going out in cakes; the river is up a foot since the 268th and brown. He says a week, as he has for a week; then why: he will not hang a boat on a cable with ice still coming down. The rope: "four-strand"; Brom is told that the far bank's first load is cordage. Tents: three fires have become seven. Seln cuts the forty-first notch and says what he expects on the first boat. Brom carries a three-legged stool down from the keeper's kitchen for the board's end.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:43:2. **The hearing (271, noon, the long board).** All of it, with the six, in daylight. Seln prices it in the registry's own terms: the gate; the book; what a certificate does when it is shown; the bag that goes to the district seat at dusk; the instrument in the drawer; what "served" means for each of four names: three papers held at a counter, and one person produced to a frame. He is not on that instrument and has another exposure of his own. Lira's certificate. Karis's. Brom's Copper. Oryn stands by the stool and will not sit in it; Lira names it the mule's. Oryn says nothing about the station. Cael says what he is afraid of and why he will not rule before the boat: a desk has had a hundred and forty-one days, and whatever it has sent is on the far bank.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:44:3. **The bench (272, morning).** Oryn's first stop after a thaw, seen from outside: the keeper's wash-house behind the inn, its door open; a bench along the wall under the eave, beyond the end of Pike's plank; who comes down out of a cold term (frost-bitten toes, a child's chest, the carter off the ice, the hide-woman's hands); the worst first; what she says to each before she touches; payment in kind; the keg and the count of fifty; grey by noon. Pike looks at a healer working off his eave without a slip. The older healer comes down the bank, looks at the knot on Brom's webbing and at Oryn, and goes up again: it is not when. Cael has the tenth and nothing to do with it, and keeps away from her bench.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:45:4. **The cloth and the wrist (272, after noon).** Pike inks the new cloth for the thaw: he carries each crew's number over; the five have none, "so I carry the place": eleventh. What the cloth is and is not. Teague's crew makes ready in the yard of the upper inn: the spear's head back on its pole; the bow's new string; the boy's pack. The older healer hands Teague a wrist; he shuts his fist and tries it on nothing. He comes down: "When?" Cael cannot tell him, and says so. The term holds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:48:## Chapter 8 — Both Hands (days 273–276; Vastin's window, 265–276) · Cael ≈2,700 · Vastin ≈2,400
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:50:1. **The square (273, first light).** The silent yard's pegs still stand in thawed turf. Lira takes the longest stave in the bundle, one that cannot be used one-handed. The healer's rule is off: "she's had her hands on all of me." Cael's ten are shut, by the yard's rule and his own. First exchange: her left hand comes a beat behind her right, so that everything from her left side arrives late; he goes in on the late side. One to him. Second: she lets go with the left and fights one-handed, as she has for a hundred and seventy days, and is too quick for him. One all. He tells her what she did.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:52:3. **The river (275–276).** The last of the shelf goes on the 275th. Ephram's letter gets its line. On the 276th the flood: the water is over the lowest plank; whole trees; the ferryman looks at it for an hour and says "Tomorrow. Light, the first time." Brom and the money that will buy no rope tomorrow.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:53:4. **Vastin (the 265th).** The last station on the east road: the ford with the wrecked ferry and its toll-board; the swept house; the register open at its ribbon and a line that stops at the fourth column; the sill between the house and the frame-house, where nobody puts out a hand for his paper. The brown coat; the stick; the knee; the flat on his back; the leaf in his coat. He steps over.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:54:5. **Vastin (the road, to the 276th).** Three people tell him to go to the plank: a courier with half a hat-brim at a ford; an old carter at a halting-ground ("You're paper"); a boy on the western landing. The broker looks him over for a hand and finds no use for him at any price. He waits for the boat with what he carries. He has read the sheet for its bar and has never weighed its date.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:58:1. **First light.** Half the meadow on the bank. Seln cuts the forty-seventh notch. The scow goes over light, with the ferryman at the sweep, and the river takes her across in a third of the time. On the far bank he loads people and waves the carts off: eight.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:60:3. **The post.** What he has and will not use, with the reasons: Pressure (narrow and deep; it would go through the ice and into nine people), Anchor (a held point costs him everything else, in full view of a bank of people who are going west, and he has held one for sixty counts once). The read, on the ground: the post's foot is going south a finger at each heave; the bank is slurry; the old sill is two strides south and worth sending a load to. Brom and one of the scow's blocking timbers. Lira and the brown mule on the second bar. Seln at the pawl. **Deployment: thirty.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:61:4. **The line.** On the scow a passenger in a brown coat lays down his stick and takes the tail of the parted strap from a carter who cannot hold it. He passes it behind his back, sets his boots against the rail-post's foot, and stands. He does not haul. He holds her upstream corner to the cable for as long as it takes to wind her home. Nothing on him changes colour; nobody on that boat declares anything. The ferryman has to tell him twice that he can let go.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:62:5. **The landing.** Cael's near sight is gone. The passenger comes up the planks; he makes the short bow to the ferryman; he pays his copper. The stance; then the face. Seln's one word. The title, and the protected answer. Lira's face for men in grey. The ferryman and his rope. Brom: nothing on him; he held it with his back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:67:1. **The doorway.** Seln has the door. The four protected lines, their first words to each other. The short bow, to the room. Who sits: Brom with the bowls, Karis, Cael, Seln at the wall; Vastin asks whose the stool is and is told; he takes the bench's end and pays for his bowl. Oryn stands. Lira stays on her feet at the hearth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:68:2. **The short thing.** He resigned, or walked out; he did not wait to be told which. No rank, no seal, no office behind him. Seln says what his trade would make of such a man. Brom's protected line. Lira sits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:77:3. **What follows him.** Seln asks. Nothing that can cross the Line: his old office wants a district to run in. Lira: six stood on a rim. His answer has "is not mine" in it. What he does not know and says he does not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:79:5. **The ferry goes west (after noon).** Ephram's letter and a copper to the boy. The carts go over, two to a crossing. No cordage comes back. Vastin on the bench under the eave with his stick and nothing to carry; Brom will not let him lift a box; Cael does not invent an errand for him. The log's line: thirty.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:86:3. **The sheet.** From the flat's lid. A technician's return. The words, set apart, verbatim, once, with a marker where the map leaves the date to the coordinator; the bar, laid with a brush. Vastin knows what such a bar is for and nothing else about the sheet. Karis copies it and writes *not read* where the bar is. Seln goes still; Cael sees it and does not know what it was; Seln does not say.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:88:5. **The lamp.** Six people. The leaf on the bare end of the table. Cael's hand a hand's width from it while a whole fill of oil burns. Nobody says the direction. Lira asks whether he has ruled; Brom goes to rope the boxes so that nobody need say it. Seln lays his wand down. The log: the 277th; thirty. Overhead, a step.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:93:- "Vastin," — Seln, ch9. · "Not that. Not for some months. Vastin will do; it did for my father." — Vastin, ch9, in answer to the title (spoken by Cael: my staging; flagged).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:94:- "What'd he do?" / "Nothing," Vastin said. "Out here. Nothing yet." / "Then he's nothing yet." — Pike, Vastin, Pike; ch9.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:95:- "You came through the board," / "I came through the board." / "Then you already know it doesn't care who you were." / "I'm learning," Vastin said. — Seln, Vastin, Seln, Vastin; ch10.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:98:- "Not *will not*. *Cannot.* There is no key." — Vastin, ch10.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:99:- "Why us." — Lira, ch11. · "Then I still haven't asked." — Oryn, ch11. · "What follows you" (Seln) and "is not mine" (inside Vastin's answer), ch11.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:101:- The close: "Because a council would file it," Vastin said, "and I spent forty years being the man they sent to make sure the filing held. I know exactly how deep a thing has to be buried before no one goes looking. This is deeper than that." [a beat of mine] "I helped bury smaller things. I'd like to dig one up before I'm done." — ch11.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:112:Says what he is afraid of at the hearing, and gives a reason for waiting that is a reason (7) · keeps the tenth away from a healer's bench (7) · tells Teague that he does not know (7) · sees Lira's left as she once saw his, and says it (8) · stops sparing her when he is told to (8) · the letter's line (8) · two fragments refused with their reasons, and the cheap one used and paid for (9) · says a title and is corrected: he had the man filed under an office (9) · lets the man answer Pike for himself (9) · keeps the borrowed room's rule at the table, and knows that it is now his own choice (10) · gives the question to Karis (11) · does not invent an errand for a man with nothing to do (11) · a hand's width, and no ruling, and no pretending (12).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:114:Supporting: Vastin 3 (the line; "nothing yet" and what he pays; the close) · Karis 2 (the receipt; a title, not a name) · Seln 2 (the doorway; the stillness) · Brom 1 (the demonstration) · Lira 2 (does not stop; sits last and asks) · Oryn 1 (has not asked) · Pike 1 (prices him at nothing yet).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:119:- **Chapter 7.** The hurdle is woven on the evening of the 272nd (not the 274th), so that the chapter runs in order and the bout follows it the next morning. The scene of the price is one continuous hearing on the 271st; Cael says that he heard the case again by daylight "the day after" the fire. Seln no longer says anything that he could not know from this bank (the five bags and the kept hour of Book 6 ch58 happened after the crew had left): the paper "has found nothing yet to take hold of", and the order's hour "fell after we were gone". Pike's season figure is written but not voiced.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:120:- **Chapter 8.** The window opens "Twelve days before that boat, when the count at Lowmarch stood at two hundred and sixty-five". Added to it: the frame-house door and the second reading that he declined (allowed to the cutaway by the map's POV table; the reason is not given); a flat cake left on a stump, and a copper that is still there in the morning. The rain on the night of the 275th and Lira's arm in the wet were added to the river scene.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:121:- **Chapter 9: the straps were renamed** so that the picture holds: the scow hangs by a **bow strap** and a **stern strap**, and it is the stern strap that parts. Her stern swings downstream on the bow strap "like a gate on one hinge". The passenger takes the torn strap's tail, passes it once round the stern rail-post and behind his own back, and sits back on it. Seln drops the drum's pawl ("an iron dog"); the tall man drives the wedge and says nothing; Teague's bow and the young one put their shoulders to the beam. The crossing home takes twenty-two minutes by Hesk's clock. The scene on the landing and the scene at the plank are two scenes; the chapter has five.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:122:- **Chapter 10.** Added: Vastin asks that it be written down ("In Ostrand I asked that nothing should be written… I ask the contrary now"); the six give him their names, Seln last; the mender and the shimmed frame, told by Vastin as his reason for believing the man; why he could not go to the archive himself (a book at its door); he asks the keeper for a bed and pays a fourth coin, and Brom adds up four and a half coppers. The chapter ends on Lira's two words.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:123:- **Chapter 11.** The table runs on without a break through the first three scenes of the plan, which are here two scenes and a third; the scene breaks fall after the knee, after Vastin's statement about the pending paper, and at the boy's cry. Added: Vastin says, from the inside, what "pending jurisdiction" is (the fourteenth chapter's ninth part; it does not lapse; he could not have lifted it); "You file a thing where it can be found again." The completion report moved out of this chapter: chapter 11 ends at "More than four" and "I am counting".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:125:- **Chapter 12.** Opens with the last sheet. Added: what a routing note is (Seln), and the tray marked *held* (Vastin); Seln's reading of a paper that arrives without its note (somebody wished him to have it, or wished to learn what he would do), which Vastin cannot decide; Vastin says that he cut the leaf from a register and that it was wrong; Blade asks *Edge?* of the cut and is told no; Karis's receipt, printed; Seln lays down his wand at forty-seven; Oryn shuts her mouth a third time (the 268th, the 271st, tonight). The stair: he takes four steps fast, stops, and goes on slowly, and nobody below can say whether it was her order or the knee.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:126:- **Nobody says the direction's name** in chapters 10, 11 or 12, in speech. The boy's cry at the landing is "Boat's going over". Seln says that the report "went over" on the hundred and second day.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/EVENT-LIST.md:128:- **The Vastin window** is 2,118 words (the map gives about 2,500).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:8:- Cael: nineteen, no birthday in this book; no Path; his own Arbiter woke at his Kindling and went dark; ten fragments; **deployment since the Line twenty-seven**; Shadow used twice and sealed; Anchor used twice (once each way); Tide: himself three times, Oryn twice by her leave, nobody else; the still place left alone by order; ribs quiet since the 129th. Both brass edges read TRUE in his hand at entry.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:9:- Lira: left arm slung high, holds nothing until Oryn says; right ankle taped, unmended, in the carter's great boot; Oryn's crossbow, hook, one bolt. Brom: right shoulder in four yards of webbing; the knot is the older healer's. Karis: Iron Rank Three; fifty-two sheets (11/29/12); the kit and the dead man's ledger; the hide with four rings and a ruled line; the Ternhall brass; her hypothesis unsaid. Seln: the case shut.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:10:- Money: ninety-six in hand; the sealed reserve apart. Owed: sixty yards of four-strand rope to the ferryman; a letter to Ephram. Pike: nine lines; the season line with no number; eleventh on the cloth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:18:## The sums that must add up on the page
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:24:- **Deployment:** 27 → **28** (140th, the Iron read on the frozen ground at the calf) → **29** (161st, the Iron read on the ice). Everything in the shed and the meadow is a trial and is not counted (as the kerb trial of the 118th was not). No self-reading. No Tide on anybody. Shadow not opened. Anchor: trials only, so "used twice, once each way" still stands.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:25:- **The yard:** forty-two strides from the plank's left-hand post to the trough at the gate, by the cord, for Karis, Lira, Brom and Seln; "forty-one and a piece" for Cael, three times.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:47:1. **The shed (131, later that morning).** The keeper will not have a mule under his eave; Cael walks Oryn's brown mule down to the ferryman's round shed, empty since the gelding went to the smith. Ice skins the shallows. The trough is frozen; Ember offers a point; he uses his heel. What he is and what the ten are, by what he refuses and what he opens: the read, on the new ice. The ferryman watches him use the shed and asks no fee. Nothing crosses until the thaw: the count has stopped.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:48:2. **The back room (131, noon).** What a cold term is. Karis has the kit's case open and will not drive stake thirty-two. Cael says what he means to do with the term: the ten, by use; under three rules (out of sight of anybody who could carry it west; Shadow shut; nothing on a person unasked). Karis: trials are entered as trials. Seln will keep the door, and says what he is counting. Karis's first piece about where an answer lies.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:49:3. **The shed (131, night).** Lira on the mounting block. The lantern lit with a point; the burn. Three bursts across the ring; one count locked each time; her correction: it is a way of leaving, so choose where to stand like a post. Shadow lifts with the dusk and is held. Seln's back in the doorway.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:57:1. **Out (138–139).** Two days on the cold road. The hold; the factor, who asks nothing but what they can do; the fence; the herd on the line; the byre underneath it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:60:4. **The calf (140, afternoon).** A calf leaves the line for the cattle's salt and puts a foreleg through a capped hole. The carters' rule broken on purpose: Cael beside it, the read on the ground; Brom's rail from the uphill side; Seln with scraped moss held high and back; Lira calling the old cow's feet. Out. His near sight gone for an hour.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:61:5. **Forty-one (141–146).** Brom reads the line of posts like a wall. Seln and two of Teague's posts; he tells only Brom; Brom re-sets them at dusk; Cael counts forty-three and does not write whose. The factor pays forty at the gate and asks no name. Home; the tenth line. Log: twenty-eight. Karis's second piece.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:68:4. **Teague's window (the night of the 148th).** The upper inn. The old woman and his wrist; the boy and the hot cloth; the boy asks leave to learn the count from the girl on the bench; Teague grants it. The light in the ferryman's shed, which he does not go down to. The cloth he cannot see from there and knows.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:74:2. **The ice (161).** The river has been a road for a week. The three on the rope-house roof. A cart cuts the bend and goes through, eighty yards out. The ferryman's rule for his ice. Cael out first with the hauling rope's end, reading.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:75:3. **The lip.** The cart hangs by its fore-axle; the carter in the water; Brom flat on his face with a fist in the man's belt; Seln at the mules. Anchor and Wind offer and are refused, with the reasons.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:76:4. **The drum.** Lira leads the brown mule round the ferry's drum; the cart comes up a plate at a time; he walks backward before it, calling the ground. Out. The bill. The ferryman.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:109:- **Chapter 3 has six scenes.** Teague's window is in two parts (the wrist and the boy; the light in the shed and the cloth). The bench has the older healer on it beside Brom and Lira; the three grey men name the square "the silent yard". **Seln's hazel wand** carries his count of the desk's days (eighteen notches on the 148th, twenty-eight on the 158th, a hundred on the 230th; a second wand at forty on the 270th); with Teague's term it is the two clocks.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:111:- **Chapter 4:** the young one asks Lira on the morning of the second bout; the tall one "calls" a touch taken by grounding the pole once; the pole is shortened to its middle and beats him three to one. On the ice one barrel is lost; Lira's part in the shed is given as told afterward. The kit scene closes the chapter (Karis opens the dead man's ledger for the first time, thirty-four days after Seln gave it to her).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:112:- **Chapter 5:** the cord is given its working (a brass eye, a knot at every fifth stride, five knots to a length, a notched slip of ash for the odd strides); Brom's hardest pull moves the figure by a thumb's breadth, the right way (short). Karis's window is in two scenes. Her interior no longer prints any part of the rule a second time. The sack game is dated the 190th. The ferryman's reminder about the rope and the mule was added before the 263rd.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md:113:- **Chapter 6** has six scenes: the log is written in the ferryman's shed on the 270th, after a look with the read at the rotten shelf (a look, not counted, as on the first morning). Nobody at the table on the 268th says the name of the direction; Cael writes it. Oryn stands at the board's end and does not take the sixth place. The ferryman's pay and fee are settled on the 268th.

